; An amount in "%" used as a posting's quantity is an ordinary commodity
; in the arithmetic behind costs, lot prices and --percent shares.  That
; arithmetic used to divide by 100 whenever "%" was its right operand,
; so 10% @ $5 cost $0.50, 985% traded for 10 BOND recorded a lot price
; of 1.015228 BOND per unit, a lot total of 50 on 10% gave a per-unit
; price of 500 rather than 5%, and --percent gave 7500.00% for 30% of
; 40%.  The percentage reading of "%" belongs to value expressions only
; (see 2724.test).

2024/01/01 Rate units bought at a price
    Assets:Rate    10% @ $5
    Assets:Cash

2024/01/02 Rate units bought for a total
    Assets:Rate    10% @@ $50
    Assets:Cash

2024/01/03 Par traded for bonds
    Assets:Par      -985%
    Assets:Bonds    10 BOND

2024/01/04 Shares
    Shares:A    30%
    Shares:B    10%
    Equity

2024/01/05 Rate units with a lot total and no commodity
    Lots:Rate    10% {{50}}
    Lots:Cash

test bal -B --flat ^Assets:Rate ^Assets:Cash
               $-100  Assets:Cash
                $100  Assets:Rate
--------------------
                   0
end test

test bal --lots --flat ^Assets:Par
-985% {0.010152 BOND} [2024/01/03]  Assets:Par
end test

test bal --percent ^Shares:
             100.00%  Shares
              75.00%    A
              25.00%    B
end test

test bal --lots --flat ^Lots:
           -10% {5%}  Lots:Cash
            10% {5%}  Lots:Rate
--------------------
                   0
end test
